+/*
+ * macOS port (ga403wm Step137): the caller says that its user range [addr, addr + size) maps IOSurface surface_id from
+ * the surface's first byte. The next userptr import of exactly that range then pins the IOSurface's own memory
+ * descriptor instead of faulting the range in through the process's map. The kernel checks the claim (the range's
+ * first page must be the surface's first page) and falls back to the plain userptr pin when it does not hold.
